#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
# Estate secret-scanning pre-push (house standard, from projects/personal/duet).
#
# DELIBERATELY LIVE — do not turn this off, and do not "fix" it back to a warning.
# Installed 2026-08-29 after a live credential was committed and pushed to this
# estate on 2026-08-25.
#
# git feeds a pre-push hook its ref list on STDIN exactly ONCE. Capture it up
# front so anything added after this point can still read it, and so "no refs"
# can be told apart from "an earlier check drained stdin".
REFS="$(cat)"
red='\033[0;31m'; yellow='\033[1;33m'; green='\033[0;32m'; nc='\033[0m'

# THE SECRET SCAN THAT USED TO SIT HERE IS GONE ON PURPOSE (2026-09-01, board).
#
# CI owns this repository's configured secret scan for pushes and pull requests.
# Scan scope and implementation vary by repository; CI is the source of truth,
# and this hook must not claim that every repository scans full history. In
# `automancer-auto`, for example, CI scans the commits added by a change.
# Scanning again here duplicates the CI check without adding protection.
#
# WHAT STILL PROTECTS THIS REPOSITORY, and it is more, not less:
#   1. `.githooks/pre-commit` runs `gitleaks git --staged` on every commit. That
#      catches a secret BEFORE it is committed, which is strictly earlier than
#      this hook could.
#   2. CI runs this repository's configured secret-scanning checks on pushes
#      and pull requests. Keep this description aligned with actual CI behaviour,
#      without naming a workflow file that may be renamed or absent elsewhere.
#
# Do NOT re-add a full-history scan here. If you are copying this hook into a
# repository that has NO secret-scan CI job, keep the scan -- the rule is that
# it runs exactly ONCE per push, in CI where CI exists and locally where it
# does not.

